{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791594950,"nonce":"NnYB2MM1LNvY+UTVzaZSfpYjPok=","message":"Authoring API and binding landed in the working tree (2026-10-10); not committed. One scope item is open.\n\nDone\n- src/native/notch.ts: a typed Notch (four signed radii, a top and a bottom edge), the edge helpers notchEdge.scoop, bulge, cut and peak, notch(), concaveTop() and the twelve-number encoding. The names avoid the corner-shape keywords scoop and notch.\n- The addon binds Scene::set_notch (NativeLayoutNode.set_notch), refusing a wrong length, an edge kind outside 0 to 4, or a negative edge.\n- LayoutNode.setNotch, HostElement.setNotch and HostElement.bindNotch, which follows a signal or computed and leaves a plain box when it ends.\n- tests/native-notch.mjs, with probes derived from the shader's geometry: a concave-top dropdown, a peak tooltip, an island scoop, a slot, a bulge and a cut; a border and an outer shadow following the silhouette; validation; a bound signal; a radius swept through zero continuously. Mutating the edge kinds, the corner order and the binding cleanup fails it each time.\n\nOpen\n- An inset shadow ignores the notch. In blinc_abi display_list.rs the inner-shadow primitive is built on the padding box and never gets the node's notch, while the outer shadows set it. The blinc_ts shadow shader already handles the notched inset case. display_list.rs is shared by both SDKs, so the owner of blinc_abi main has been asked whether to change it; the test for it is not written, so it will not pass for the wrong reason.\n- No CSS property for a notch yet (open question above).\n- The border test relies on borders taking layout space (blinc_abi 3db5b2d and the css-paint branch), which the notch's body inset does not know about: content needs padding for both.","files":null}]}